<title>USA: Salomon CPI-linked bond upped to $450 mln.</title>
<headline>Salomon CPI-linked bond upped to $450 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Inc's issue of inflation-indexed five-year notes was increased by $50 million to $450 million, according to lead underwriter Salomon Brothers on Friday.</p>
<p>The issue was initially increased from $250 million.</p>
<p>The debt was given a 3.65 percent coupon and priced at 99.04 to yield 3.88 percent, or 65 basis points over the U.S. Treasury's 10-year inflation-indexed bond.</p>
<p>The deal is rated Baa1 by Moody's Investors Service and BBB by Standard &amp; Poor's.</p>
<p>((U.S. corporate bonds unit, 212-859-1672))</p>
